Temporary instrumentation of `uedcli-native/src/permeating_lights.rs` used to measure how often the
retired sign-sum heuristic disagreed with `FPlane(A,B,C)`'s own orientation, and why. Apply on top of
the landed code (which no longer has the heuristic) to re-measure; NOT applied in the tree.

`PROBEWIND` checks the portal-winding invariant the fix rests on: every stored portal poly's winding
normal must oppose `Portal.normal`. `PROBEFLIP` fires where the retired heuristic would have negated
the plane, and prints the offending clip edge's length -- which is what showed every disagreement to
be a degenerate (sub-2.5e-4-unit) edge.

--- a/uedcli-native/src/permeating_lights.rs
+++ b/uedcli-native/src/permeating_lights.rs
@@ leaf_portal_map, right after `let normal = Vec3::new(p.normal[0], ...);`
+        {
+            let wn = verts[1].sub(&verts[0]).cross(&verts[2].sub(&verts[0]));
+            if wn.dot(&normal) >= 0.0 {
+                PROBE_WIND_BAD.fetch_add(1, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed);
+            } else {
+                PROBE_WIND_OK.fetch_add(1, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed);
+            }
+        }

